<title>USA: Shiva Corp Q2 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Shiva Corp Q2 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>BEDFORD, Mass. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				Jun 28,     Jun 29,   Jun 28, Jun 29,</p>
<p>				  1997	   1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		   $39,738     $51,485   $70,897 $94,794</p>
<p> Cost of revenues	  15,949	21,397    37,588  38,782</p>
<p> Gross profit		23,789	30,088    33,309  56,012</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p> Research &amp; development   5,778	 5,462    11,739  10,656</p>
<p> SG&amp;A			  20,409	16,801    38,307  31,506</p>
<p> Merger expenses		---	 1,987	 ---   1,987</p>
<p> Total operating expenses 26,187     24,250    50,046  44,149</p>
<p>Income</p>
<p>  (loss) from operations(2,398)	 5,838  (16,737)  11,863</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	  (996)	 4,975   (9,366)   9,314</p>
<p> Net EPS		     (0.03)	  0.16    (0.32)    0.30</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs	     29,128	32,067    29,050  31,296</p>
<p>		(unaudited, in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q2 1996 net income includes $2.0 million or $0.06 a share of expenses related to acquisition of Airsoft Inc.</p>
<p>1997 six month period results ended June 28, 1997 include the effects of Q1 charges related to price protection reserves and inventory writedowns, which negatively hurt Q1 EPS by $0.28.</p>
